"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIt's well known as a regular spot for the late Chung Ju-yung, honorary chairman of Hyundai Group, who enjoyed it so much that he would visit by helicopter whenever he was in Gangwon-do.  \nAlthough the main restaurant is in Gangwon-do, I visited with confidence as it's a branch that inherited the same flavor.  \n\nThe mul-makguksu (cold buckwheat noodles in broth) is said to be characterized by its mild taste.  \n\nHowever, I was more in the mood for bibim-makguksu (spicy buckwheat noodles) that day, so I ordered two.  \nNaturally, I ordered one as a double portion.  \nI also ordered a buckwheat pancake.  \n\nI ordered a double portion based on the typical amount of makguksu in Seoul, but I was surprised by how generous the portion was.  \nIt probably wasn't necessary to order a double portion. But I finished it all anyway.  \n\nThe spicy seasoning for the bibim was hotter and more stimulating than expected, but it was delicious.  \nThe buckwheat pancake had a rich aroma and was delightfully chewy.  \n\nFor reference, other regulars were ordering boiled pork slices (suyuk), so I'll have to try that next time I visit.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n"